# Build-context exclusions for Railway / Railpack.
#
# Railpack reads this file and passes the patterns to BuildKit, so anything
# listed here never enters the build context or the deployed image.
#
# Rationale: the repository tracks ~542 MB, and the directories below are
# reference material and local scratch output that the application never
# reads at build time or at runtime. Shipping them forces the image-packing
# stage to copy hundreds of megabytes for no benefit.
#
# NOTE: public/uploads/ is deliberately NOT excluded here. It is ~196 MB of
# customer files that prod-server.cjs still falls back to on disk when a file
# is not yet in the database. Excluding it needs the object-storage migration
# to land first.

# Version control and CI metadata
.git
.github
.githooks

# Replit-specific runtime config (Railway does not read these)
.replit
replit.nix
.replit_integration_files
.agents
.canvas

# Reference material and scratch output — not read by the app
attached_assets
previews
screenshots
exports
audit
docs
*.png
*.PNG
*.jpg
*.JPG

# Dependencies and build output (reinstalled/regenerated by the builder)
**/node_modules
.cache
.local
.upm
.pythonlibs
dist

# Local environment and editor files
.env
.env.*
.vscode
.idea
*.log
